{
  "title": "Third declension: things and ideas",
  "note": "Third-declension gender by ending: -tas (veritas, veritatis) is feminine; -or (amor, amoris) mostly masculine; -men (nomen, nominis) and -us with genitive -oris or -eris (tempus, temporis) neuter. Neuters have nominative = accusative and plural -a: corpora. Tempus, corpus, caput, nomen and mare are neuter; lex, pax, mors, nox, lux, urbs and virtus are feminine.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Dickinson College Commentaries, Latin Core Vocabulary",
    "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/latin-core-list1"
  },
